    setMemory(prev => obs.status === "dismissed" ? prev.filter(o=>o.id!==id) : prev.map(o=>o.id===id?obs:o));
    return obs;
  } catch { pushToast(...); return null; }
}, [pushToast]);

const deleteObservation = useCallback(async (id) => { await apiDeleteObservation(id); setMemory(prev=>prev.filter(...)); }, [pushToast])
```
Wait: deleteObservation is an explicit delete (not used by UI? UI uses dismiss via update status). Keep.

```ts
const clearMemory = useCallback(async () => {
  await apiClearMemory();
  setMemory([]);
  setConversationId(null);
}, [pushToast]);
```
Since server deletes conversations too. Also messages? If we clear memory, should we clear the thread? The design says clearing memory also clears conversation id (server deletes both). We should clear messages too? If server deleted the conversation, keeping messages displayed is okay but they'll be orphaned; next message creates a new conversation. But the UI says "Forget everything", which should probably clear the thread as well for coherence. Hmm. The spec says clear memory removes observations and conversations. I'll also reset messages to [] to match (and close panel). But that could surprise. Let's do it: `setMessages([])`. Actually "Forget everything" in the memory panel means forget what it learned; wiping the visible conversation is expected if server deletes it. I'll clear messages.

