clearChat: abort, setMessages([]), setConversationId(null), and create a new conversation:
```ts
void apiCreateConversation().then(c => setConversationId(current => current ?? c.id)).catch(()=>undefined);
```
Hmm: after clearChat, we set conversationId null, then create returns id and sets it. If the user sends before it resolves, sendMessage closure uses conversationId from the render at call time (null), server creates a new conversation, SSE sets it; then the create promise may resolve and overwrite with the empty one unless functional guard. Use `setConversationId(current => current ?? conversation.id)` so real SSE id wins. Good.

