parts.text:
Add CSS for memory-edit and memory-add. Then Task 7.

CSS:
```css
.memory-edit { display flex column gap 8px; }
.memory-edit__input, .memory-add textarea, .memory-add select { width:100%; padding:8px 10px; border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:8px; background:var(--bg-raised); color:var(--text); font: inherit; font-size: .86rem; }
.memory-add {...}
.memory-add__field { display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:6px; font-size:.78rem; color:var(--muted);}
```

Also `.memory-item__head .memory-item__actions { margin-top: 0; }`.

Then Task 7: test first in UiRenderer.test.tsx. Add test:

```tsx
it("renders an opportunity thesis with the bet and the next move", () => {
  renderSpec({
    type: "opportunity-thesis",
    props: {
      title: "Own activation without a guided setup",
      importance: 9,
      satisfaction: 3,
      gap: "New users stall on the first empty state.",
      thesis: "We treat setup as a checklist when people need a first win.",
      next_move: "Prototype a one-step first win and test it with five new accounts.",
    },
  });

  expect(screen.getByLabelText("Opportunity thesis: Own activation without a guided setup")).toBeInTheDocument();
  expect(screen.getByText("New users stall on the first empty state.")).toBeInTheDocument();
  expect(screen.getByText("We treat setup...")).toBeInTheDocument();
  expect(screen.getByText("Prototype...")).toBeInTheDocument();
  expect(screen.getByText("Underserved · 15.0")).toBeInTheDocument();
});
```

Component:
```tsx
export function OpportunityThesis({ node }: NodeProps) {
  const title = str(node.props, "title");
  const importance = num(node.props,"importance",0);
  const satisfaction = num(node.props,"satisfaction",0);
  const gap = str(node.props,"gap");
  const thesis = str(node.props,"thesis");
  const nextMove = str(node.props,"next_move") || str(node.props,"nextMove");
  const score = scoreOf(node.props);
  return (
    <article className={`ui-card ui-card--thesis${isUnderserved(score)?" ui-card--urgent":""}`} aria-label={`Opportunity thesis: ${title}`}>
      <header className="ui-card__head">
        <span className="ui-card__id">Opportunity thesis</span>
        <ScorePill tone={bandTone(score)}>{bandLabel(score)}</ScorePill>
      </header>
      <h4 className="ui-card__title">{title}</h4>
      <div className="ui-card__meters">
        <MeterBar label="Importance" value={importance} tone="info" />
        <MeterBar label="Satisfaction today" value={satisfaction} tone={bandTone(score)} />
      </div>
      {gap ? <p className="ui-thesis__gap"><b>The gap:</b> {gap}</p> : null}
      {thesis ? <blockquote className="ui-thesis__claim"><Markdown source={thesis} /></blockquote> : null}
      {nextMove ? (
        <aside className="ui-callout ui-callout--info">
          <div className="ui-callout__body">
            <div className="ui-callout__title">Next move</div>
            <Markdown source={nextMove} />
          </div>
        </aside>
      ) : null}
      <ActionRow actions={readActions(node.props)} />
    </article>
  );
}
```
Check `ui-callout__title` exists in primitives. Yes likely. Search quickly. Also `ui-card__title`. Fine.

Catalog entry before decision-record:
```ts
entry(
  "opportunity-thesis","leaf",
  "One opportunity argued in plain language: the scores, the gap, the thesis, and the next move. Use when the PM is deciding what to chase.",
  {
    title: {type:"string"},
    importance: {...},
    satisfaction: {...},
    gap: {type:"string", description:"The customer or business gap in one sentence."},
    thesis: {type:"string", description:"Why this is the opportunity worth winning, in plain words."},
    next_move: {type:"string", description:"The smallest concrete step to test it."},
  },
  ["title","importance","satisfaction","thesis"],
),
```
Registry.

CSS for thesis: use existing classes mostly; add `.ui-card--thesis .ui-thesis__claim` styling and `.ui-thesis__gap`. Let me check existing `ui-card--outcome` styles for guidance.

